Fillets: the piece where a ball rolling on an edge turns about the edge's
vertex onto the next edge is walked back only over its turn and oriented
as its neighbours (mitcad#343).

The case: 0904's notch walls, whose far edges are in pieces (the wall's
edges with the tongue's faces): the ball rests on their common vertex
while its other contact moves on (a contact that stands still, 0200), and
then rolls on the next edge. Three faults there:

- ChFi3d_Builder::ComputeData (a surface and an edge): a walk back from the
  start of the piece walked before it, starting on such a vertex, was
  completed forward from its start (as a walk from inside the spine is),
  over the piece before it, up to where its contact reached an edge 0.2
  further: overlapping pieces, an invalid result. Such a walk is not
  completed forward.
- ChFi3d_ExtendAtSpineEnds extended a piece at the end its walk started
  from, where its section is the one the piece before it ended with; only
  the end the walk reached is extended now.
- ChFi3d_FilDS: the side of a piece reduced to a point (the vertex the ball
  turns about) took its transition from the walk, from a contact that does
  not move: the turn's face came out reversed on its wire
  (BRepCheck_BadOrientationOfSubshape). It takes the transition of a
  neighbouring piece on the same faces rolling on the same edge (a
  neighbour that rolls on no edge there, as at 0390's concave turn, is
  passed over).

Upstream: new.

